WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.361
Dwayne Johnson and the Marvel Cinematic Universe
seem like a natural fit for each other, and

00:00:05.361 --> 00:00:08.100
yet, the Rock has yet to appear in an MCU
movie.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.160
So what gives?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.540
Although it may seem strange that the hottest
star in Hollywood hasn’t starred in a Marvel

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.100
movie, there are few reasons that could explain
why.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.780
In 2014, it was announced that Dwayne Johnson
would be joining the DCEU, portraying the

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.060
villainous Black Adam in a Shazam movie.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.520
Many were surprised that the Rock was playing
a bad guy rather than a superhero, with the

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.380
assumption being that the larger-than-life
actor would prefer to be the star of his own

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.380
DCEU film.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.820
Those predictions ultimately proved correct.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.700
If you've seen Shazam!, which was released
in April 2019, then you know Johnson isn't

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:41.200
in it.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:46.480
That's because, after meeting with DC brass
in 2017 to discuss his role, it was announced

00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:48.999
that Black Adam was getting his own solo movie.

00:00:48.999 --> 00:00:53.420
The film has no release date yet, but it's
still very much in the works, and it's expected

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.140
to start filming in 2020.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:00.059
The fact that Johnson will be headlining a
DCEU movie greatly reduces his chances of

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:04.620
doing the same for Marvel, because, well,
it's pretty rare for actors to star in films

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.800
for both franchises.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.840
And when they do, it's generally as side characters
moving from one franchise to another in a

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:15.680
bigger role; remember when Shazam's Zachary
Levi played Fandral in two out of three Thor

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.180
films?

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.700
We've yet to see a lead actor switch teams,
but here's hoping Johnson might be the first.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.960
The Rock likes to refer to himself as the
hardest worker in the room, and it's not just

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:26.820
a catchphrase.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.760
The guy works all the time.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.180
Take a look at his Instagram feed, which he
updates constantly, and you'll see he's always

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.860
either shooting a movie or doing press for
a movie.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.500
The man just moves from one project to the
next non-stop.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.040
In 2018, he starred in two blockbusters with
Rampage and Skyscraper.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:49.860
In 2019, he headlined Fast &amp; Furious Presents:
Hobbs &amp; Shaw and Jumanji: The Next Level,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.880
while also appearing in Fighting with my Family,
whose production he spearheaded.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.000
"What are your names again?"

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:55.700
"My name— "

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.680
"It doesn't matter what your names are!

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.180
You walk around here interrupting The Rock,
you, like you haven't seen the sun in twenty

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:01.680
years.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.680
You, like you just stepped out of Oliver Twist!"

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.819
Next year, Johnson's got Disney's Jungle Cruise
and action comedy Red Notice, co-starring

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.850
his DCEU stablemate Gal Gadot.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.360
He also stars on HBO's Ballers, hosts a reality
competition he created called The Titan Games

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:20.630
on NBC, and has quite a few films in various
stages of production.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.890
Plus, he's active as a producer on multiple
movies, he's working on releasing a tequila,

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.920
and he's helping design products for his Project
Rock collaboration with Under Armour.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.020
Plus, he's working out like a beast and raising
a family.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:38.520
2016's People's Sexiest Man Alive is Busy
with a capital "B," and chances are good that

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.680
he simply hasn't had the time to work a Marvel
movie into his crazy schedule yet.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.660
Some actors just look tailor-made for their
roles.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.180
Has there ever been a more James Bond-looking
James Bond than Pierce Brosnan?

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.850
Can you think of a more appropriate man to
play the Mountain on Game of Thrones than

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.640
actual World's Strongest Man Thor Bjornsson?

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.400
And when it comes to superheroes, who's more
qualified to play one than real life superhuman

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.740
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson?

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.060
The Rock has a physique that looks like it
was drawn by Rob Liefeld, so it seems like

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.920
a no-brainer that he should find himself a
spot in the MCU.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:14.110
The only problem is, Marvel prefers to go
with the unexpected when it comes to their

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.340
superhero casting.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:20.220
When the studio needed to cast Star-Lord,
the suave leader of the Guardians of the Galaxy,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.080
they didn't go out and get Chris Pine or James
Marsden.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.000
They went with Chris Pratt, who at the time
was best known as a somewhat schlubby sitcom

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:28.500
actor.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.840
They also went with funnyman Paul Rudd for
Ant-Man, relative unknowns Chris Hemsworth

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:38.550
and Tom Hiddleston for Thor and Loki, respectively,
and they cast the supposedly washed-up, over-the-hill,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:43.580
and problematic Robert Downey Jr. as Iron
Man, the guy who ended up leading the entire

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.580
franchise.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.880
And although Marvel sometimes does what's
expected, the studio may think that casting

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.400
the Rock as a superhero is a little too on
the nose for their brand.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.960
As his level of stardom has grown over the
last handful of years, so has the Rock's level

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.300
of influence in Hollywood.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.820
Seven Bucks Productions, the studio Johnson
founded with his ex-wife Dany Garcia in 2012,

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:09.260
has produced every single movie the actor
has starred in since 2017's Baywatch.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.800
Not only that, but Johnson wields a considerable
amount of power over those films.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.180
He's very cautious about maintaining his image,
and he's known to be pretty inflexible when

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.420
it comes to certain aspects of his films.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.020
For example, he forced a change to the ending
of Rampage so the gorilla wouldn't die at

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:25.520
the end.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:30.100
Plus, he broke away from his role in the Fast
and Furious franchise to lead his own spinoff,

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.100
Hobbs &amp; Shaw.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:31.740
"One!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:32.920
Two!

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:33.440
Three!"

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.740
"No one tells me what to do!"

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.400
Johnson has shown that he likes to be in control
of his films, and if there's one studio that's

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.140
not known for giving up control, it's Marvel.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.260
With the exception of the Spider-Man movies,
which are produced in coordination with Sony

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:53.550
Pictures since they own the film rights to
the character, Marvel Studios doesn't share

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.850
production credit with any other studio.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:05:01.290
The studio's president, Kevin Feige, has the
final say on everything in the MCU, and Johnson

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:05.370
may not be willing to cede the control he's
become accustomed to just for a spot in a

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.360
Marvel movie.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:11.380
In spite of all the factors working against
the Rock joining the MCU, it still seems like

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.800
there may be something going on between them
that we just don't know about yet.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.440
At the 2019 MTV Movie Awards, Avengers: Endgame
director Anthony Russo joked that Johnson

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.940
should join the MCU…as himself.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.990
But the most compelling piece of evidence
comes in the form of a throwaway line Johnson

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:32.190
included in a congratulatory message he shared
to Instagram to celebrate Endgame's box office

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:32.760
success.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:37.260
The Rock gushes about Marvel in his three-minute
video, showing nothing but love for the studio

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:42.210
and name-dropping a lot of people integral
to its success including Nebula actress and

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:45.120
his, quote, "Jumanji partner in crime, Karen
Gillan."

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.900
But the biggest name drop had to be Kevin
Feige, the head honcho at Marvel Studios.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.720
"Congrats, and I know our assistants have
been trying to get us together for dinner

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:53.800
for months now.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.880
We're both super busy boys, and I look forward
to our schedule linking up."

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.960
Can you smell what the Rock is cooking there?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:04.050
If we had to guess what these two busy boys
would talk about over dinner, first on the

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.540
agenda would have to be the prospect of Johnson
joining Team Marvel.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:12.360
Just because the Rock hasn't appeared in the
MCU yet doesn't mean he's not going to eventually.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.840
After all, someone's going to have to play
the Thing when Fantastic Four inevitably gets

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:17.380
rebooted.

